# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# Node
node_modules/

# Build
dist/
build/

# VS Code
.vscode/

# Real résumé corpus — contains real names/phones/emails, never commit.
# "test_corpus/*" (not "test_corpus/") so the directory entry itself isn't
# excluded -- a blanket directory ignore can't be un-ignored from inside,
# only its contents can.
test_corpus/*
*.pdf
*.docx
*.oxps

# ...but the synthetic fixtures and the corpus README must be committed
!backend/tests/fixtures/pdfs/**
!test_corpus/README.md

# ESCO skills taxonomy (Phase 1 item 2): ~9.5MB external dataset, not repo
# content -- see backend/data/README.md for the fetch command. The
# 92-term seed taxonomy (skills_seed.json) stays committed; it's the
# bootstrap set tests and CI depend on.
backend/data/skills_en.csv
backend/data/*.zip

# skillNer (Phase A extractor benchmark) writes these into the CWD as a
# side effect of importing skillNer.general_params -- runtime artifacts,
# not repo content. See services/skills/extractors.py.
backend/skill_db_relax_20.json
backend/token_dist.json

# evaluation/step0/Resumes/: 39-resume calibration set, all template/
# placeholder identities verified individually (e.g. "(xxx) xxx-xxxx",
# "hello@reallygreatsite.com" -- Canva's own template placeholder domain,
# "555.555.5555") -- no real names/contact info, safe to commit, and this
# is the human-labeled evaluation asset the whole scoring calibration
# effort depends on.
!evaluation/step0/Resumes/**